// regexp_ast_ref_smoke — `regexp/syntax`'s AST, stage 2a of §2c.
//
// `Regexp` is what the parser produces and the compiler consumes.
// Stage 1 gave the RE2 construction its instruction array; this gives
// it the tree that lowers into one. Neither is wired to the live
// matcher — see the module header for why the swap is last.
//
// The trees here are not hand-written. The reference dumps each parsed
// tree as an s-expression and a generator turns THAT into the Rust
// constructors below, so the two sides cannot drift by a typo. Doing
// it by hand has already cost this port one false divergence.
//
// What is actually being checked is `String()`, and it is a harder
// function than it looks: Go does not print the pattern it was given,
// it prints a CANONICAL form, and reaching one means a whole
// flag-placement pass. `calcFlags` walks the tree computing which of
// `(?i` `(?m` `(?s` must and cannot be active around each node, finds
// the conflicts, and inserts spans; `writeRegexp` then renders them.
// Four rows show it working:
//
//   (?i)[a-z]     -> [A-Za-zſK]      the fold is compiled INTO the
//                                    class, and the two extra runes
//                                    are the Kelvin sign and long s
//   (?i)a|(?-i)b  -> (?i:a)|b        the span is inserted, not copied
//   \Q+|*\E       -> \+\|\*          quoting is resolved at parse
//   $             -> $, \z -> \z     same Op, told apart only by the
//                                    WasDollar flag — which is also
//                                    the one flag `Equal` compares
//
// 280 rows from `scripts/goref.sh regexp/syntax
// tools/gen_regexp_ast_ref.go`.

